launchpad/docs/documentation-review/test_documentation_review.py  strengthening a check that could not fail: the MD/YAML parity scan used the generator's own regex, so a one-char edit dropped an item from BOTH sides and the suite passed (found by cross-model review). Making the test's scan deliberately looser than the generator's so the two can disagree, and adding real content parity. This makes the suite stricter, not greener.
